.SH NAME
CWE\-653 \- Improper Isolation or Compartmentalization
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product does not properly compartmentalize or isolate functionality, processes, or resources that require different privilege levels, rights, or permissions. When a weakness occurs in functionality that is accessible by lower\-privileged users, then without strong boundaries, an attack might extend the scope of the damage to higher\-privileged users.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB1\fR exploited CVE mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2025\-21590
Juniper Junos OS, added 2025\-03\-13.
.PP
Juniper Junos OS Improper Isolation or Compartmentalization Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Juniper Junos OS contains an improper isolation or compartmentalization vulnerability. This vulnerability could allows a local attacker with high privileges to inject arbitrary code.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply mitigations per vendor instructions, or discontinue use.
 Due 2025\-04\-03.
.PP
